a16z-mercury-banking-for-startups:greenh.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Senior Workday Analyst to help take our rapidly growing organization to the next level. At Mercury, we are investing in modernizing and optimizing our HR technology landscape, streamlining processes, and building a foundation that can support continued expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will report to our Head of People Operations and serve as a strategic partner to HR, Payroll, and business leaders, leveraging deep Workday expertise to streamline processes, automate manual work, and enhance the employee experience across the organization. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who enjoys complex challenges, and wants to influence the future of HR Operations by identifying innovative solutions, implementing best practices, and leveraging Workday technology to create more efficient, scalable, and employee-centric experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are some things you’ll do on the job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, maintain, and optimize Workday Core HCM, Payroll, and Absence modules to support business processes and organizational requirements. Provide support for additional Workday modules as requested.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain compliance with federal, state, and local payroll regulations and absence policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Workday reports, dashboards, and analytics related to payroll and absence data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Workday security for new implementations, acquisitions, reorganizations, and system enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams and third-party vendors on processes and integrations impacting payroll, time tracking, benefits, and absence management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document system configurations, procedures, testing, recommendations for optimal system setup and migration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audits, reconciliation activities, and year-end processes as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR, Payroll, and business stakeholders to evaluate, implement, and maximize AI-driven solutions within Workday and related HR technologies, driving innovation, process optimization, and scalable operational improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Information Systems, Business Administration, Finance, or related field (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Workday functional experience, including configuration and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years supporting HCM, Payroll and Absence or Time Tracking modules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in complex organizations with multiple business units, local and international employee populations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payroll calculations, earnings, deductions, garnishments, and tax setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configuration and maintenance of leave plans, accruals, eligibility rules, and absence validations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Workday business processes, organizations, staffing models, and worker lifecycle events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configuration of time entry codes, work schedules, overtime rules, and time calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total rewards package at Mercury includes base salary, equity (stock options), and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary and equity ranges are highly competitive within the SaaS and fintech industry and are updated regularly using the most reliable compensation survey data for our industry. New hire offers are made based on a candidate’s experience, expertise, geographic location, and internal pay equity relative to peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our target new hire base salary ranges for this role are the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US employees in New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area: $154,200 – $192,800 USD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US employees outside of New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area: $138,800 – $173,500 USD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Canadian employees (any location): CAD 145,800 – 182,200&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Mercury are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities or special needs. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CJ1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

a16z-stripe:greenhouse:7394627.descriptionHtml:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Iberia Enterprise team works with the region&#39;s most ambitious market leaders and high-growth innovators to help them build the financial infrastructure that powers their next stage of growth. As trusted business partners, we bring deep product expertise and a consultative approach — partnering with companies across retail, travel, fintech, and beyond to unlock new revenue streams and drive global expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure is transforming how businesses in Iberia operate, automate, and scale. This is a pivotal moment for Stripe in the region — the market opportunity is significant, and our team serves as a critical source of user feedback and market intelligence, with direct influence on the product roadmap and growth strategy. We&#39;re a collaborative, curious team looking for a hunter who&#39;s eager to open new doors and build lasting relationships in one of Europe&#39;s most dynamic markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Hunter Account Executive covering new business, you&#39;ll identify new opportunities to expand Stripe&#39;s footprint. Specifically, we&#39;re looking for someone who executes on long-term sales strategies, engages with internal and external stakeholders, aligns on technical and business requirements with product teams, builds value in competitive situations, leads commercial negotiations, and closes deals within the Enterprise space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand business with high-growth technology companies and traditional enterprises&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from prospecting to close, partnering with cross-functional teams along the way (SDR, Product Sales, Solutions Engineering, and Risk and Legal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own account mapping and coordinate effective meetings with appropriate external stakeholders to expand the customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Regional Partnerships team to drive brand awareness and pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sales experience, selling a highly technical product to enterprise customers, with a track record of top performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units across complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Spanish and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of people, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in and knowledge of technology, the payments landscape, and related products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

a16z-stripe:greenhouse:7417090.descriptionHtml:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developer Experience and Product Platform (DEeP) org empowers all of Stripe&#39;s products with a shared product platform that can help with rapidly delivering high-quality, consistent, cross-product experiences across our UI and API surfaces. It focuses on providing a consistent and scalable developer experience that any developer can leverage to accelerate a customer&#39;s ability to create value from Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an experienced Technical Program Manager to join our Organization Access Platform (OAP) team, focusing on security initiatives. In this role, you&#39;ll drive critical security programs across multiple teams, manage dependencies, and ensure the successful delivery of security features that protect our platform and users. This is a highly technical role requiring strong program management skills and the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your role involves spearheading large-scale technical programs, solving intricate challenges, and ensuring successful product launches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end program management for critical security initiatives including API key security, Account Takeover (ATO) prevention, login access controls, and other risk, security, and fraud prevention measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-team dependencies and collaboration between security, fraud operations, and product engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, communicate, and resolve program blockers across multiple workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop implementation roadmaps and execution strategies for complex security features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering managers to define technical requirements and prioritize security enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish metrics and reporting processes to measure program effectiveness and security outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate decision-making processes when trade-offs arise between security, user experience, and development timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent OAP security initiatives in cross-functional meetings and leadership reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program management experience with demonstrated success in security-focused initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex technical programs with multiple stakeholders and dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of security concepts and best practices, particularly in API security, authentication systems, and access controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to translate complex technical concepts to various audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of influencing decisions across teams without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with engineering and product teams in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent practical experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment systems, financial technology, or enterprise SaaS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of compliance requirements related to data security (SOC2, PCI, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with identity and access management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in API development or platform security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working on developer platforms or developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7460470.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Software Engineering builds the brains of Waymo&#39;s fully autonomous driving technology. Our software allows the Waymo Driver to perceive the world around it, make the right decision for every situation, and deliver people safely to their destinations. We think deeply and solve complex technical challenges in areas like robotics, perception, decision-making and deep learning, while collaborating with hardware and systems engineers. If you’re a software engineer or researcher who’s curious and passionate about Level 4 autonomous driving, we&#39;d like to meet you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this hybrid role you will report to a Technical Lead Manager, Senior Staff Engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership for onboard motion planning systems that improve low-speed maneuvering performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve evaluation capabilities to better understand on-road performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide mentorship for junior engineers on the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate driving behavior issues from logs and understand the root cause&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop foundational frameworks that help advancement of the Waymo Driver&#39;s capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to solving some of the most challenging driving situations in the long tail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS/PHD in Computer Science, ML, Robotics, similar technical field of study, or 4+ years of equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General software engineering experience programming in C++ with robust and efficient code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate within and across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year of management experience years with 5+ reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AV or Robotics experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Machine Learning models in production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in graph search, optimization, or path planning algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Software Engineering experience in complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding proficiency in Python and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$238,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$302,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7671186.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Hardware Engineering is an innovative and collaborative group of electrical, mechanical, reliability, software and vehicle engineers. We design, build, and perfect the products which are the eyes and ears of Waymo&#39;s autonomous driving technology, and integrate those products into vehicle platforms. We&#39;re seeking curious and talented teammates to keep us moving in the right direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and reports to the Director, PCO Programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;ew8ZDf kYh61e&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within HW Engineering, responsible for program management of Waymo’s future generations of Self Driving Systems (SDS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a full system architecture lifecycle of a new generation of hardware - from concept/architecture to production launch while developing roadmaps for future generations of SDS programs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate deeply with cross-functional teams within HW Engineering (Vehicle, Component and Module Design, Validation, Systems, Manufacturing) and partner teams (Software, Operations, Product) to plan and execute critical SDS programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage integrated program schedules, balancing technical requirements, design, validation, budget, and market deployment needs to ensure on-time delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution of these SDS programs. Identify, manage and overcome challenges through the product development process from start-to-finish including leading problem solving with relevant technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly build and maintain deep technical knowledge of autonomous driving components and their system-level interactions to inform program priorities, guide technical discussions, and drive progress with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A BS or MS degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Science or a similar discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years practical hardware engineering experience (electrical and mechanical) in product development and&lt;br&gt;5+ years in program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of systems integration, new platform &amp;nbsp;launch process and critical path management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated strong analytical, oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to effectively influence and communicate cross-functionally and within a matrix organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical abilities - able to work closely/credibly with highly technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in the product development process, understanding and execution from &amp;nbsp;prototype to production (Design, Build, Validate, Production)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in system or vehicle integration preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in robotics or autonomous driving vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$248,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7932205.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are building a team of engineers dedicated to further developing our in-car experience. &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Projects include the Pick Ups and Drop Offs (PUDO) experience, and Infotainment during passenger trips (music, games, maps). Our team works on the user interfaces used by customers to hail and control our autonomous vehicles. We build complex user experiences, phone-to-vehicle communications, and solve novel human-computer interaction problems in the AV space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to an Engineering Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will: &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Set the overarching technical architecture, defining a multi-year technical vision across the entire in-car experience (ICX), bridging the gap between the different layers of the stack, from low-level hardware bring-up to our OS to rider-facing apps and features.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Identify broad, cross-team bottlenecks (e.g., OS stability, rendering performance, release automation), and translate them into clear, actionable engineering milestones for the teams to execute on that improve both velocity and stability. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Steer the technical integration of complex, high-impact features, such as our 3D car view, AI features, and in-car app ecosystem. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Act as a force multiplier for the organization by establishing high standards for code health, system reliability, and testing excellence, while providing deep technical mentorship to junior and senior engineers. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Make significant individual contributions in both design and code to ensure we can land the technically challenging work needed for this space to succeed, from implementing large changes to investigating tricky bugs. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Proven experience as a technical lead with a track record of setting strategic technical direction and delivering concrete solutions for complex, multi-team domains.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience working with Android/AOSP (building Android platform features, frameworks), not just developing apps on top of Android&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Deep expertise spanning the modern application and embedded stack, specifically involving Android OS internals, C++ native layers, and modern UI frameworks (Kotlin, Jetpack Compose), as well as complementary backend systems.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong system design skills with a demonstrated ability to decouple monolithic architectures, build reusable platform infrastructure, and optimize resource-constrained environments.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Exceptional communication and cross-functional leadership skills, capable of influencing without direct authority to build alignment across Product, UX, Systems Engineering, and Hardware teams.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;AI-native mindset with a proven track record of deploying agent systems to improve team velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Familiarity with automotive context with Android.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience establishing frameworks for third-party experiences.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience integrating new hardware features into an extensible framework for 1P and 3P usage.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$298,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$368,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7766502003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;font-semibold&quot;&gt;About You and The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Zipline is looking for an exceptional Executive Assistant to support our CEO and help keep the company operating at the highest level. This is not a traditional administrative support role. The CEO’s office sits at the center of Zipline’s most important priorities, relationships, decisions, and operating rhythms. The person in this role will help create leverage, clarity, and momentum for the CEO while working closely with senior leaders across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;You will be trusted with highly sensitive information, complex priorities, and fast-moving decisions. You’ll need strong judgment, discretion, ownership, and the ability to operate with context rather than waiting for step-by-step direction. The right person is calm under pressure, exceptionally organized, direct in communication, and energized by being close to the work that shapes the future of the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;This role requires someone who can anticipate needs before they are obvious, protect the CEO’s time, improve how information flows, and ensure that important commitments do not get lost in a high-velocity environment. You should be comfortable working with executives, board members, investors, external partners, government stakeholders, and internal teams with professionalism and precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;This role is based at our South San Francisco, CA headquarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;font-semibold&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Partner directly with the CEO to manage time, priorities, commitments, and operating cadence with a deep understanding of company goals and business context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Own and optimize a highly complex calendar, using judgment to prioritize the highest-impact meetings, protect focus time, and ensure the CEO is prepared for critical conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Act as a trusted point of coordination between the CEO and internal leaders, helping drive follow-through on decisions, deadlines, and key initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Prepare the CEO for meetings by gathering context, organizing materials, tracking open questions, and ensuring the right people and information are in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Manage highly sensitive communications and information with absolute discretion, sound judgment, and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Coordinate board, investor, customer, partner, and external stakeholder engagements, ensuring every interaction is thoughtfully planned and executed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Plan and manage complex domestic and international travel, including detailed itineraries, logistics, meeting preparation, and contingency planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Help run key leadership forums, executive meetings, offsites, and company operating moments by managing agendas, logistics, materials, notes, and follow-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Proactively identify friction in the CEO’s workflow and improve systems, processes, and communication loops that create better leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Represent the Office of the CEO with clarity, warmth, and high standards in interactions across the company and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;font-semibold&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;7+ years of experience supporting a CEO, founder, or senior executive in a high-growth, high-standards environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Exceptional judgment and discretion, especially when handling confidential, sensitive, or strategically important information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Strong business instincts and the ability to understand priorities, tradeoffs, and urgency without needing every detail explained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to be clear, concise, professional, and direct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;High ownership and follow-through. You notice what needs to happen, take responsibility for it, and drive it to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Outstanding calendar, travel, and logistics management skills, including experience supporting executives with highly dynamic schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Ability to operate calmly in ambiguity and make good decisions when priorities shift quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Strong relationship skills and executive presence, with the ability to work effectively across senior leaders, board members, investors, partners, and employees at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Impeccable attention to detail and a strong instinct for preparation, quality, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;A service-oriented mindset paired with backbone. You are helpful, thoughtful, and proactive, while also comfortable pushing back and protecting priorities when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Energy, resilience, and enthusiasm for working in a mission-driven company where the pace is fast and the work matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;font-semibold&quot;&gt;What Else You Need to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $150,000 - $250,000. Please note that this is a target starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash payment for this role will depend on various factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may include equity compensation; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; benefits such as medical, dental, and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex, including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;_markdownText_1ni73_69 _paragraph_1ni73_65&quot;&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like this position&#39;s sound but are unsure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7776545003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About You &amp;amp; the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is scaling new markets, operating systems, and launch infrastructure that only work if analytics, execution, and operating cadence stay tightly connected. We are looking for a Strategic Operations Manager who can build the mechanisms that help leadership see clearly, make decisions, and drive execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional PM role. You will move fluidly between building forecasting models, running operating reviews, coordinating cross-functional initiatives, identifying bottlenecks, and creating the systems that allow teams to scale. The mandate is simple: be a builder, not a coordinator.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own recurring operating rhythms and business reviews that turn leadership priorities into clear owners, dates, metrics, tradeoffs, and follow-through. You will make sure commitments are visible, decision points are crisp, and action items move from discussion to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and maintain planning, forecasting, and capacity models; develop dashboards and reporting that improve decision quality; diagnose operational bottlenecks; and drive cross-functional initiatives from ambiguity to execution across technical and non-technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will create scalable systems and processes that improve organizational effectiveness as Zipline launches, scales, and operates new markets. That includes turning one-off efforts into repeatable mechanisms without adding bureaucracy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-10 years of experience in operations, business operations, strategic planning, manufacturing, logistics, supply chain, program management, or another execution-heavy operating environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and modeling skills, with the ability to build practical tools that leaders and operators actually use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication; you can turn ambiguous work into clear narratives, decisions, and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across technical and non-technical teams, align stakeholders, and drive accountability without hiding behind process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated history of creating systems that scale: operating cadences, planning models, dashboards, review mechanisms, ownership models, and follow-up loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguity and high-growth environments where the right answer changes as the business learns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High execution discipline; you can build a model in the morning, facilitate an executive review in the afternoon, and drive action items to closure by the end of the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Else You Need to Know&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be an in-office role based out of our South San Francisco HQ. Must be able to travel up to 25% of the time either to our HQ or into the Field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $112,500 - $300,000; please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. We are always open to negotiation. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; overtime pay; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;

abstractvc-alpaca:greenhouse:5701700004.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered self-clearing broker-dealer and brokerage infrastructure for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more. Our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alpaca.markets/blog/alpaca-raises-150-million-at-a-1-15b-valuation-to-build-the-global-standard-for-brokerage-infrastructure/&quot;&gt;recent Series D funding round&lt;/a&gt; brought our total investment to over $320 million, fueling our ambitious vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 9 million brokerage accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;opening financial services to everyone on the planet&lt;/strong&gt;. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by top-tier global investors, including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Unbound, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 380+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Your Role:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;As a Site Reliability Engineer (SRE) at Alpaca, you will ensure the reliability, scalability, and performance of our systems and services. You will work closely with development, operations and devops teams to build and maintain robust applications, ensuring they run smoothly and efficiently. This role requires a blend of software engineering and operations skills, with a strong ability to troubleshoot technical issues and resolve problems before they impact our users.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Triage difficult technical problems and implement solutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Improve our observability stack (monitoring, logging, profiling)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Incident Management: Respond to and resolve incidents in a timely manner, conducting post-incident reviews to identify and implement improvements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Collaboration: Work closely with development teams to ensure new features and services are designed with reliability and scalability in mind.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Capacity Planning: Monitor system capacity and performance, making recommendations and implementing changes to handle future growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Who you are (must-haves):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering, Performance Engineering, or similar roles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience with multi-terabyte scale PostgreSQL clusters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Proven track record of managing and maintaining large-scale, high-availability, and high-performance PostgreSQL database.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience designing and implementing SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs for internal systems and databases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with troubleshooting PostgreSQL performance problems and slow queries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Extensive experience with efficient schema design and efficient query design.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience migrating multi-terabyte tables into more efficient schemas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Proficient with Go.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Proficient with Prometheus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Proficient with Linux.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Knowledgeable in trading/fintech domains.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with low-latency systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with distributed tracing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience scaling PostgreSQL clusters rapidly.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with pgx, gorm, or sqlc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

adventinternational-ebanx:greenhouse:765.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EBANX&lt;/strong&gt; is the leading payment platform connecting global companies with customers from the fastest-growing digital markets in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since the beginning of our journey, we have had one mission: to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;provide global access&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for everyone. We believe that transforming challenges into opportunities and making the impossible part of the journey is crucial! That&#39;s precisely why we created a payment technology that builds bridges between people and businesses every day in 29 rising markets across the globe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We call ourselves ebankers, we are global thinkers, we value diversity, we foster creativity and we work hard to connect businesses and people worldwide through payments. Let&#39;s make history together?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are searching for a Senior Analyst for North Cone who will be responsible for&amp;nbsp;supporting teams in Mexico, Colombia, Central America and Caribbean on important&amp;nbsp;operational tasks driving business efficiency. This includes, but is not limited to:&amp;nbsp;managing administrative duties, local campaigns, monitoring fees, benchmarking local&amp;nbsp;data via local relationships and market intel. It is important to have a solid background in&amp;nbsp;the financial, payments, eCommerce and tech industries; and proven established&amp;nbsp;relationships within the local payments ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;1s0186q&quot; data-start=&quot;173&quot; data-end=&quot;211&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;175&quot; data-end=&quot;211&quot;&gt;You will also be responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;212&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;116hw4j&quot; data-start=&quot;212&quot; data-end=&quot;506&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;214&quot; data-end=&quot;506&quot;&gt;Own administrative tasks such as supporting invoice processing, purchasing processes, vendor payments, coworking bookings, vacation tracking, expense management, sending legal agreement templates and NDAs, and other administrative activities to ensure smooth local and financial operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1wjj8mv&quot; data-start=&quot;507&quot; data-end=&quot;610&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;509&quot; data-end=&quot;610&quot;&gt;Ensure operational process flows and SLAs are properly defined and implemented with local partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;18n07xw&quot; data-start=&quot;611&quot; data-end=&quot;782&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;613&quot; data-end=&quot;782&quot;&gt;Monitor fees (e.g., chargebacks, retries), manage cost inputs in internal databases, and support merchant category code (MCC) validation and value-added cost tracking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;19g8soh&quot; data-start=&quot;783&quot; data-end=&quot;1014&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;785&quot; data-end=&quot;1014&quot;&gt;Support compliance with card scheme and regulatory mandates by tracking scheme rules and creating follow-up action plans with Product and Regulatory teams to ensure EBANX and merchant readiness for new requirements and changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;4m6ipn&quot; data-start=&quot;1015&quot; data-end=&quot;1134&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1017&quot; data-end=&quot;1134&quot;&gt;Manage and support marketing campaigns with local providers, partners, global merchants, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1hcxb8r&quot; data-start=&quot;1135&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1137&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;Support Country Managers with market intelligence (product, regulatory, and performance insights), leveraging strong local relationships with partners and providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;1304&quot; data-end=&quot;1307&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;5h6vgl&quot; data-start=&quot;1309&quot; data-end=&quot;1350&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;1311&quot; data-end=&quot;1350&quot;&gt;Main requirements for this position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1351&quot; data-end=&quot;2115&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;62nm00&quot; data-start=&quot;1351&quot; data-end=&quot;1389&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1353&quot; data-end=&quot;1389&quot;&gt;Native Spanish and fluent English.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;d6q3fh&quot; data-start=&quot;1390&quot; data-end=&quot;1483&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1392&quot; data-end=&quot;1483&quot;&gt;Proven background in the financial services, payments, eCommerce, or technology industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
